rewritten-to-match
Same ray tracer, expression by expression in the reference's order: normalize is a scale by 1.0 / magnitude, dot products add left to right, the first sphere a ray hits wins (the reference's break), shading is the same clamp, light scale and 0.3 object colour, the character is picked by floor(level * 6). The reference's Vector/Color/Sphere/Light structs are scalars and per-sphere arrays; the ray origin is the zero vector, so adding and subtracting it is left out (it does not change any result; Rust folds the subtraction as well). Pixels are character codes added to the checksum rather than characters. Stores are checked and undo-logged (the loop's accumulator is a local, stored once per run).
